Package: bGMYC4
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian General Mixed Yule-Coalescent Model for Species
        Delimitation
Version: 4.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Noah", "Reid", email = "noah.reid@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cph"), comment = "Original author of bGMYC"),
    person("Dmitry", "Karabanov", email = "dk@ibiw.ru",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6008-7441"))
  )
Description: Implements a Bayesian version of the general mixed
    Yule-coalescent (GMYC) model for species delimitation from
    single-locus data (Reid & Carstens 2012, BMC Evolutionary
    Biology 12:196). Markov Chain Monte Carlo sampling evaluates
    the posterior distribution of species boundaries under flexible
    uniform priors, with branching rates profiled at their maximum
    likelihood estimates. Supports pooling over multiple posterior
    trees to propagate phylogenetic uncertainty into marginal
    probabilities of conspecificity, convergence diagnostics
    (split-Rhat, ESS, prior-vs-posterior contraction), and
    interactive heatmap visualization of the resulting matrices.
